{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי יפול הנופל", :translit "ki yipol ha-nofel", :gloss "when one falls, the one who falls"} {:he "לא תזרע", :translit "lo tizra", :gloss "you shall not sow"} {:he "עד שיזרע חטה ושעורה וחרצן במפולת יד", :translit "ad she-yizra chitah u-se'orah v'charutzan bi-mefolet yad", :gloss "until one sows wheat, barley, and grape seed by hand-planting"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut ha-parshiyot: the adjacency of 'you shall not sow' (Deut 22:9) to 'when one falls' (Deut 22:8) signals that the 'fall' refers to agricultural sowing"}], :frame {:text "R. Yoshiya disagrees with R. Yonatan over the scope of the prohibition of kil'ayim (diverse kinds). R. Yoshiya restricts it to conventional sowing of wheat, barley, and grape seed together; R. Yonatan extends it even to non-standard planting methods. The phrase 'במפולת יד' (hand-planting) is drawn from the language of Sifrei on this verse. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the proximity of לא תזרע to כי יפול הנופל as a scriptural hinge connecting these two paragraphs.", :sources ["Sifrei Devarim 229" "Sifrei Devarim 230"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut ha-parshiyot: the adjacency of 'you shall not sow' (Deut 22:9) to 'when one falls' (Deut 22:8) signals that the 'fall' refers to agricultural sowing", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:13.326082979Z", :model "glm-5.2"}